```

This already guards against the exact scenario you're describing — once `open - now` goes non-positive (i.e. the window has opened), it short-circuits to the string `'WINDOW OPEN'` before the day/hour math ever runs, so negative values can't reach the render. I confirmed this isn't just a paper reading: I ran the identical logic in Node against the real system clock (currently 2026-09-20, well past the hardcoded June 15 open date) and it correctly returns `'WINDOW OPEN'`, not a negative day count. I also checked for a second/duplicate implementation (mobile view, dead code, etc.) — there isn't one; `StageMeter`, `TransferCard`, and `StoryCard` don't do any date math at all.

